ude Code did not load its part that starts the browser helper. Type /${jFt} (if it tells you to run it with --force, do that), then /claude-test. If that changes nothing, the usual cause is another enabled Claude Test plugin. In /plugin, open the Installed tab. Leave ${$3} (builtin) on. If the tab lists another Claude Test plugin, disable that one. Then, or if there is none, restart Claude Code.`,zr=`To start Claude Test, type /claude-test in the terminal where Claude Code is running. If that does not start it, or from Remote Control, type /${jFt} first, then /claude-test.`,Kr="Claude Test is still getting ready. Type /claude-test in a moment.";function Yr(e){return`Claude Test cannot run in this session: another enabled plugin is also named claude-test and loads first: ${e}. Disable or uninstall that one on the Installed tab of /plugin. Leave ${$3} (builtin) on. Then restart Claude Code.`}var Fe="Claude Test's browser helper is not ready in this session. Type /claude-test to start it and run the tests.",qr="Claude Test could not start its test agent in this session, so nothing ran. Type /claude-test to try again. If this message comes back, restart Claude Code.",Ht=`Claude Test did not start: its test agents are not loaded in this session. Type /${jFt} (if it tells you to run it with --force, do that), then /claude-test. If this message comes back, restart Claude Code.`,jt="Claude Test did not start: its test agents are still loading. Type /claude-test in a moment.",Jr="Claude Test did not start: its test agents were loaded just now. Type /claude-test to run it.",ut="Claude Test is not available in this session right now, so it did not run. If you just changed your login, wait a moment, then type /claude-test again. If you see this message again, restart Claude Code; if it still shows, Claude Test is not available here.",ct="Claude Test did not run: the Claude Code login or plan changed since its browser helper started, or could not be checked, so the helper was stopped. Type /claude-test to start it again.",Me="Claude Test did not start: it could not check the Claude Code login. Type /claude-test to try again. If this happens again, sign in again with /login, or restart Claude Code.",Pn="Claude Test is not ready yet: its browser helper connected, but its tools did not show in time. Run /claude-test. If the helper was only slow to start, that will work.",Ln=`Claude Test did not start: its browser helper is switched off for this project. Type /${jFt} (if it tells you to run it with --force, do that), switch ${GJ} on in /mcp, then run /claude-test.`,On=`Claude Test did not start: this session does not connect its browser helper (${GJ}). The cause is how this session was started, or a setting for MCP servers. To see which, start claude with --debug, run /claude-test, and read the line about $.mcp.connect in the debug log (in ~/.claude/debug). If the setting is your organization's, only your administrator can change it.`,kn="Claude Test did not start: its browser helper did not come up. Run /claude-test. If the helper was only slow to start, that will work. If it keeps failing, check that node is installed, and see /mcp for the error; you can reconnect the helper there, then run /claude-test.",Wt="Claude Test did not start: Claude Code would not connect its browser helper in this session. Restart Claude Code and run /claude-test. If that fails too, start claude with --debug, run /claude-test, and read the line about $.mcp.connect in the debug log (in ~/.claude/debug); it says why.",Nn="Claude Test did not start: another MCP server in this session already runs Claude Test's browser helper. In /mcp, switch off the server whose Command ends in playwright-mcp.mjs, then run /claude-test.",In="Starting the Claude Test browser helper.",vn="Claude Test did not start its browser helper: this build of Claude Code cannot check its files, so it starts nothing. Please report this.";function Cn(e,n,r){switch(n){case"differs":return`Claude Test